B.Sv={family:0,numbers_time:1,dates:2,food_shopping:3,places:4,home:5,phrases:6,everyday:7,work:8,housing:9,health:10,travel:11,adjectives:12,formal:13,society:14,verb_position:15,conjugation:16,accusative:17,dative:18,modal_verbs:19,questions:20,separable:21,possessives:22,prepositions:23,negation:24,perfekt:25,praeteritum:26,subordinate:27,comparison:28,two_way_prep:29,reflexive:30,imperative:31,relative:32,konjunktiv2:33,passive:34,connectors:35,genitive:36,infinitive_zu:37,tenses:38,adjective_endings:39,verb_prep:40,indirect_questions:41,read_notices:42,read_messages:43,read_ads:44,read_details:45,read_gist:46,listen_dialogues:47,listen_announcements:48,listen_messages:49,listen_numbers:50,listen_detail:51}
B.a7c=new A.bo("Family words","Learn family words in pairs: Mutter/Vater, Gro\xdfmutter/Gro\xdfvater, Bruder/Schwester, Eltern/Gro\xdfeltern.","Die Mutter von meiner Mutter ist meine Gro\xdfmutter (Oma).","Draw your family tree and label every person in German.")
B.a7n=new A.bo("Numbers, prices & time",'German says the ones before the tens (47 = siebenundvierzig). "halb drei" means 2:30, not 3:30.',"Es ist Viertel nach sieben. Das kostet drei Euro f\xfcnfzig.","Say every price and clock time you see today out loud in German.")
B.a7D=new A.bo("Days, months & dates",'Learn the days in order (Montag \u203a Sonntag) and use "am" with days: am Montag.','Der Kurs ist am Dienstag. In \xd6sterreich sagt man oft "J\xe4nner" f\xfcr Januar.',"Write your week plan in German, one line per day.")
B.a6W=new A.bo("Food, drinks & shopping","Group words by category (Obst, Getr\xe4nke, M\xf6bel) so odd-one-out questions become easy.","Apfel, Banane und Orange sind Obst. Ein Stuhl ist ein M\xf6belst\xfcck.","Write your next shopping list in German.")
B.a7C=new A.bo("Places in town","Link each place to what you do there: B\xe4ckerei \u203a Brot, Apotheke \u203a Medikamente, Haltestelle \u203a Bus.","Ich kaufe Brot in der B\xe4ckerei.","Make flashcards: place on one side, activity on the other.")
B.a7s=new A.bo("Home & rooms","Learn rooms with their article and one activity: die K\xfcche (kochen), das Bad (duschen).","Ich koche in der K\xfcche.","Walk through your home and name every room and object in German.")
B.a6T=new A.bo("Greetings & everyday phrases","Match the greeting to the time and situation: Guten Morgen / Guten Abend / Gute Nacht (going to bed).",'Am Abend sagt man "Guten Abend". In \xd6sterreich h\xf6rt man oft "Gr\xfc\xdf Gott".',"Use one new phrase in each German conversation this week.")
B.a7a=new A.bo("Everyday words","Learn verbs together with typical nouns: Durst \u203a trinken, Hunger \u203a essen, m\xfcde \u203a schlafen.","Ich habe Durst. Ich m\xf6chte etwas trinken.","Describe your day in five simple German sentences every evening.")
B.a7o=new A.bo("Work & jobs","Know the job-search chain: Stellenanzeige \u203a Bewerbung \u203a Vorstellungsgespr\xe4ch \u203a Arbeitsvertrag.","Ich habe mich beworben und warte auf ein Vorstellungsgespr\xe4ch.","Read three German job ads and underline the key words.")
B.a79=new A.bo("Housing & renting","Kaltmiete = rent without heating/water; Warmmiete includes them; Kaution = deposit; Mietvertrag = lease.","Die Kaltmiete betr\xe4gt 500 \u20ac, die Warmmiete 650 \u20ac.","Read flat ads online and explain each one in a German sentence.")
B.a7e=new A.bo("Health & body","Learn the key places and things: Arzt, Krankenhaus, Apotheke, Rezept, Fieber, Termin.","Ich habe Fieber. Ich gehe zum Arzt.","Role-play booking a doctor's appointment in German.")
B.a7k=new A.bo("Travel & transport","Learn travel documents and transport words together: Visum, Reisepass, Fahrkarte, Gleis, Haltestelle.","F\xfcr die Reise brauche ich ein Visum.","Plan an imaginary trip in German: ticket, platform, times.")
B.a6Z=new A.bo("Opposites & adjectives","Learn adjectives as opposite pairs: billig/teuer, p\xfcnktlich/versp\xe4tet, warm/kalt.","Das Hotel ist teuer, aber das Hostel ist billig.","Write ten opposite pairs from memory, then check them.")
B.a74=new A.bo("Formal language & useful phrases",'Formal letters end with "Mit freundlichen Gr\xfc\xdfen"; give opinions with "Meiner Meinung nach \u2026".',"Meiner Meinung nach ist Homeoffice praktisch.","Write a short formal email (to a landlord or office) and check the opening and closing.")
B.a7v=new A.bo("Society & official matters",'Know common "life in Germany" words: anmelden (B\xfcrgeramt), Umwelt, M\xfcll trennen, Beh\xf6rde.',"Nach dem Umzug muss ich mich beim B\xfcrgeramt anmelden.","Read one short German news article a day and note five new words.")
B.a7q=new A.bo("Verb in second position","In a statement the conjugated verb is always in position 2, even when the sentence starts with time or place.","Am Wochenende spiele ich Fu\xdfball.","Take five sentences and rewrite each starting with a time word.")
B.a7m=new A.bo("Verb endings",'ich -e, du -st, er/sie/es -t, wir -en, ihr -t, sie/Sie -en. Learn "sein" and "haben" by heart.',"Wir wohnen in Wien. Wie alt seid ihr?","Conjugate three verbs a day out loud, all six persons.")
B.a77=new A.bo("Articles & accusative","Only masculine changes in the accusative: der \u203a den, ein \u203a einen, kein \u203a keinen.","Ich habe einen Bruder. Ich kaufe den Tisch.",'Write "Ich habe / Ich brauche \u2026" with ten masculine nouns.')
B.a7r=new A.bo("Dative","After helfen, danken, gefallen and after mit, bei, von, zu, nach, aus: dem (m/n), der (f), den + n (pl).","Ich helfe dem Mann. Ich fahre mit dem Bus.",'Make ten sentences with "mit" + a vehicle or a person.')
B.a7f=new A.bo("Modal verbs","Modal verb in position 2, infinitive at the end. ich/er forms have no ending: ich kann, er kann.","Ich kann heute nicht kommen. M\xf6chtest du Tee?","Say what you can, must and want to do today with k\xf6nnen, m\xfcssen, wollen.")
B.a7l=new A.bo("Question words","Wo = where, Woher = where from, Wann = when, Wer = who, Was = what, Wie viel = how much.","Wo wohnst du? \u2013 In Hamburg.","Interview yourself: write and answer one question with each W-word.")
B.a6X=new A.bo("Separable verbs","The prefix goes to the end of the sentence: abfahren \u203a Der Zug f\xe4hrt um 8 Uhr ab.","Ich stehe um 7 Uhr auf.","Describe your morning routine using aufstehen, anziehen, einkaufen.")
B.a7_=new A.bo("Possessive words","her = ihr, his = sein. The ending follows the noun: ihr Mann, ihre Tochter, mein Auto.","Das ist Anna. Ihr Mann hei\xdft Peter.","Describe a friend's family using sein/ihr.")
B.a7y=new A.bo("Prepositions of time & place","am + day, um + clock time, im + month; aus + country (origin), nach + city/country (direction).","Ich komme aus Indien. Der Kurs beginnt am Montag um 9 Uhr.","Write five sentences about your week with am, um, im.")
B.a6U=new A.bo("nicht or kein",'"kein" negates nouns with ein/no article; "nicht" negates verbs, adjectives and the rest.',"Ich habe keine Kinder. Ich komme heute nicht.","Answer ten yes/no questions negatively, choosing nicht or kein.")
B.a7d=new A.bo("Perfekt: haben or sein",'Use "sein" with movement or change (gehen, fahren, kommen); most other verbs use "haben".',"Gestern bin ich ins Kino gegangen. Ich habe viel gearbeitet.","Tell what you did yesterday in five Perfekt sentences.")
B.a7i=new A.bo("Pr\xe4teritum of sein, haben & modals","war, hatte, konnte, musste, wollte \u2014 these are used in Pr\xe4teritum even in speech.","Als Kind konnte ich nicht schwimmen.","Write about your childhood with war, hatte, konnte.")
B.a78=new A.bo("Word order after weil / dass","After weil, dass, wenn, ob the conjugated verb goes to the very end.","Ich komme nicht, weil ich krank bin.",'Answer "Warum \u2026?" questions with full weil-sentences.')
B.a6P=new A.bo("Comparisons","Comparative = adjective + -er + als (often with umlaut): gro\xdf \u203a gr\xf6\xdfer als.","Berlin ist gr\xf6\xdfer als M\xfcnchen.","Compare two cities you know in five sentences.")
B.a7t=new A.bo("Two-way prepositions","Movement/direction (Wohin?) \u203a accusative; position (Wo?) \u203a dative: auf den Tisch / auf dem Tisch.","Ich lege das Buch auf den Tisch. Das Buch liegt auf dem Tisch.","Describe where things are in your room, then where you put them.")
B.a6Q=new A.bo("Reflexive verbs","sich freuen, sich interessieren \u2026 : ich \u203a mich, du \u203a dich, er/sie \u203a sich.","Ich freue mich auf den Urlaub.","Learn five reflexive verbs with their preposition (freuen auf, interessieren f\xfcr).")
B.a76=new A.bo("Imperative",'du-form: take the du-verb, drop -st and "du": du machst \u203a Mach!',"Mach bitte das Fenster zu!","Give a friend five polite instructions in German.")
B.a6S=new A.bo("Relative clauses","The relative pronoun takes gender from the noun and case from its own clause: helfen + dative \u203a dem.","Das ist der Mann, dem ich geholfen habe.","Join two short sentences into one with der/die/das ten times.")
B.a72=new A.bo("Konjunktiv II (wishes & conditions)","Use h\xe4tte, w\xe4re, k\xf6nnte, or w\xfcrde + infinitive for unreal situations.","Wenn ich mehr Zeit h\xe4tte, w\xfcrde ich mehr reisen.",'Finish the sentence "Wenn ich in Deutschland w\xe4re, \u2026" five ways.')
B.a7u=new A.bo("Passive","werden + Partizip II. Past: wurde + Partizip II.","Das Haus wurde 1950 gebaut.","Describe how something is made (Tee, Brot) in the passive.")
B.a70=new A.bo("Connectors (obwohl, trotzdem, deshalb)",'"obwohl" starts a clause with the verb at the end; "trotzdem/deshalb" sit in position 1 with the verb next.',"Obwohl es regnet, gehen wir spazieren. Es regnet. Trotzdem gehen wir spazieren.","Write the same idea twice: once with obwohl, once with trotzdem.")
B.a71=new A.bo("Genitive (wegen, trotz)","After wegen/trotz use genitive: des (m/n) + noun-s, der (f/pl). Adjective ending: -en.","Wegen des schlechten Wetters f\xe4llt das Spiel aus.",'Explain five cancellations: "Wegen des/der \u2026 f\xe4llt \u2026 aus."')
B.a6R=new A.bo("Infinitive with zu",'After Lust haben, versuchen, vergessen \u2026 : "zu" + infinitive at the end; separable verbs put zu inside (einzukaufen).',"Ich habe keine Lust, heute einkaufen zu gehen.",'Make sentences with "Ich habe vergessen, \u2026 zu \u2026".')
B.a7z=new A.bo("Past perfect (Plusquamperfekt)",'hatte/war + Partizip II for what happened before another past action, often with "nachdem".',"Nachdem er gegessen hatte, ging er schlafen.","Tell a short story using nachdem + Plusquamperfekt.")
B.a7B=new A.bo("Adjective endings","After ein (neuter, nom./acc.) the adjective shows the gender: ein neues Auto; after the: das neue Auto.","Ich w\xfcnsche mir ein neues Auto.","Describe five things you own with an adjective + ein/eine.")
B.a7A=new A.bo("Verbs with prepositions","Learn verb + preposition as one unit: warten auf, sich freuen auf, denken an, sich interessieren f\xfcr.","Ich warte auf den Bus.","Make flashcards with the verb on one side, preposition + case on the other.")
B.a7p=new A.bo("Indirect questions",'Keep the question word (wann, wo, wie) or use "ob" for yes/no, and put the verb at the end.',"K\xf6nnen Sie mir sagen, wann der Zug abf\xe4hrt?",'Turn ten direct questions into polite "K\xf6nnen Sie mir sagen, \u2026" questions.')
B.a7x=new A.bo("Signs & notices","Scan for days, times and small words that change meaning: nur, nicht, geschlossen, au\xdfer Betrieb, frei.",'"Sa 8\u201312 Uhr" means the shop is open only until noon on Saturday.',"Photograph German signs online (or around you) and explain each in one sentence.")
B.a75=new A.bo("Messages & emails",'First find who writes and why. The reason often follows "leider", "weil" or "da".','"Ich bin leider krank und kann nicht kommen" \u203a the person cancels.',"Read short German emails and write the purpose in five words.")
B.a7j=new A.bo("Adverts","Look for price, time, conditions and limits: nur, ab, nicht n\xf6tig, VB (price negotiable).",'"Nur Abholung" = you must pick it up yourself; no delivery.',"Compare three ads for the same thing and pick the best one in German.")
B.a6V=new A.bo("Finding details in info texts","Read the question first, then find the exact line. Answers are often paraphrased, not copied.",'"Die Lebensmittel sind im Kurspreis enthalten" = you do not buy the food yourself.',"Do one timed reading task a day: question first, then text.")
B.a73=new A.bo("Main idea & opinions (B1)",'Do not match single words. Match the meaning of the whole sentence \u2014 and watch for "jedoch", "aber", "andere".','"Viele sparen Zeit \u2026 Andere vermissen den Kontakt" \u203a there are pros and cons.','After each article, write one sentence: "Der Text sagt, dass \u2026".')
B.a7g=new A.bo("Everyday conversations","Read the question and the three answers before the audio starts, then listen only for that piece of information. Speakers often change their mind \u2014 the last plan counts.",'"Um drei? \u2014 Nein, lieber um vier." \u203a the answer is vier, not drei.',"Listen to one short A1/A2 dialogue a day (Goethe \xdcbungssatz audio), pause after each line and say what you heard.")
B.a7b=new A.bo("Announcements (station, shop, radio)","Announcements are often played only once. Listen for numbers, places and changes: Gleis, Versp\xe4tung, statt, heute nur.",'"Der Zug f\xe4hrt heute von Gleis sieben statt Gleis drei." \u203a the platform is 7.',"Watch the Deutsche Bahn / \xd6BB announcement videos and write down platform, time and delay.")
B.a7h=new A.bo("Phone messages","A voicemail always has who, why and what to do next. Note the key detail (time, number, place) while you listen the first time, check it the second time.",'"Bitte rufen Sie mich bis Freitag zur\xfcck." \u203a call back before Friday.',"Ask a friend to leave you a 20-second German voice message and write down the three key facts.")
B.a6Y=new A.bo("Numbers & times by ear",'German says the ones before the tens (vierundzwanzig = 24) and "halb acht" is 7:30. Write numbers down as digits while you listen.','"Die Telefonnummer ist null-eins-sieben-zwei \u2026", "um Viertel nach neun" = 9:15.',"Play a German number dictation video for 5 minutes a day and write every number you hear.")
B.a7w=new A.bo("Longer talks & opinions (A2\u2013B1)","Paraphrase is normal: the audio rarely uses the words of the answer. Listen for meaning and for signal words like aber, trotzdem, eigentlich, leider.",'"Eigentlich wollte ich mit dem Auto fahren, aber \u2026" \u203a the speaker did not take the car.','Listen to one short Deutsche Welle "Langsam gesprochene Nachrichten" item a day and summarise it in one sentence.')
